\
We are now implementing the complete UI/UX for the marketplace.\
\
IMPORTANT:\
Do not modify or redesign the existing backend/payment architecture. This task is focused on the frontend UI, UX, routing, reusable components and responsive design.\
\
The application is built with:\
- React\
- Vite\
- Tailwind CSS\
- Firebase Authentication\
- Firestore\
- Firebase Cloud Functions\
- NOWPayments\
\
The website should feel like a sophisticated, premium macOS Terminal interface while remaining a modern, intuitive web application.\
\
==================================================\
1. CORE DESIGN CONCEPT\
==================================================\
\
The visual identity should be inspired by macOS Terminal.\
\
The user should feel like they are interacting with a highly polished terminal application, but the website must still behave like a normal modern marketplace.\
\
The terminal aesthetic is the BRAND LANGUAGE, not a gimmick.\
\
Use:\
\
- Dark/near-black background\
- Monospace typography\
- Terminal prompts\
- macOS traffic-light window controls\
- Terminal-style panels\
- Command-inspired labels\
- Structured tables\
- Status indicators\
- ASCII-inspired branding\
- Thin borders\
- Subtle green accents\
- Minimal animations\
- Technical/developer aesthetic\
\
Do NOT make it look like a generic cyberpunk website.\
\
Avoid:\
- Matrix rain\
- Skulls\
- Excessive neon\
- Excessive glow\
- Fake hacking animations\
- Excessive glitch effects\
- Unnecessary 3D effects\
- Clutter\
- Overly complicated interactions\
\
The interface should feel:\
- Premium\
- Technical\
- Minimal\
- Secure\
- Sophisticated\
- Fast\
- Professional\
\
==================================================\
2. VISUAL LANGUAGE\
==================================================\
\
Primary background:\
\
#050505\
\
Secondary surfaces:\
\
#0A0A0A\
#0D0D0D\
\
Primary terminal green:\
\
#00FF66\
\
Use green primarily for:\
- Active states\
- Success\
- Available products\
- Terminal prompts\
- Important actions\
\
Blue:\
- Links\
- Interactive elements\
- Secondary actions\
- Information\
\
Yellow:\
- Warnings\
- Pending states\
\
Red:\
- Errors\
- Failed states\
- Destructive actions\
\
Purple:\
- Product categories and secondary metadata\
\
Do not use these colors excessively.\
\
Typography should be monospace.\
\
Preferred fonts:\
- JetBrains Mono\
- IBM Plex Mono\
- SF Mono\
\
Fallback:\
monospace\
\
