==================================================\
4. TWO MAIN EXPERIENCES\
==================================================\
\
The website has two distinct experiences.\
\
A. PUBLIC EXPERIENCE\
For users who have not registered or logged in.\
\
B. AUTHENTICATED MARKETPLACE EXPERIENCE\
For registered/logged-in users.\
\
Do not force unauthenticated visitors into the dashboard interface immediately.\
\
The homepage should work as a proper public landing/marketing page.\
\
==================================================\
5. PUBLIC HOMEPAGE\
==================================================\
\
Route:\
\
/\
\
The homepage is the main public-facing marketing page.\
\
It should introduce the marketplace and allow visitors to understand the platform before registering.\
\
The homepage should contain these sections:\
\
1. Navigation\
2. Hero\
3. Featured Products\
4. How It Works\
5. Why Choose Us / Platform Benefits\
6. About\
7. Security / Payment Information\
8. FAQ\
9. Call To Action\
10. Contact\
11. Footer\
\
These should be sections on the homepage rather than unnecessarily creating separate pages.\
\
==================================================\
6. PUBLIC NAVIGATION\
==================================================\
\
Desktop navigation should have a terminal-inspired appearance.\
\
Example:\
\
[ BRAND ]       About   How It Works   Products   FAQ   Contact\
\
                                      [ Login ]\
                                      [ Register ]\
\
The navigation should remain minimal.\
\
When the user scrolls, the navbar can become sticky.\
\
Use smooth scrolling for homepage sections.\
\
Example anchors:\
\
#about\
#how-it-works\
#products\
#faq\
#contact\
\
The navigation should still maintain the terminal aesthetic.\
\
==================================================\
7. HOMEPAGE HERO\
==================================================\
\
The hero should immediately communicate:\
\
- What the platform is\
- What users can access\
- Why it is different\
- Clear CTA\
\
Use a terminal prompt.\
\
Example:\
\
root@marketplace:~#\
\
WELCOME TO [BRAND]\
\
A secure marketplace for premium digital products.\
\
[ Browse Products ]\
[ Create Account ]\
\
Include subtle terminal cursor/typing effects only where appropriate.\
\
Do not make the hero excessively animated.\
\
==================================================\
8. FEATURED PRODUCTS\
==================================================\
\
Show selected products directly on the homepage.\
\
Terminal-inspired presentation.\
\
Example:\
\
$ ls featured-products\
\
ID    PRODUCT             CATEGORY        PRICE\
01    Product A           Development     $49\
02    Product B           Design          $29\
03    Product C           Marketing      $19\
\
Each product should have a clear:\
\
[ VIEW PRODUCT ]\
\
button.\
\
The product data should eventually come from Firestore.\
\
Do not hardcode architecture-dependent business logic into the UI.\
\
==================================================\
9. HOW IT WORKS\
==================================================\
\
Create a simple four-step section:\
\
01 SELECT\
Choose a digital product.\
\
02 CREATE\
Create or access your account.\
\
03 PAY\
Complete payment through the secure payment flow.\
\
04 ACCESS\
Once payment is verified by the backend, access is granted.\
\
Represent this visually like a terminal process:\
\
$ initialize_purchase\
\
[1] SELECT\
[2] PAY\
[3] VERIFY\
[4] ACCESS\
\
Keep the explanation understandable to normal users.\
\
==================================================\
10. ABOUT SECTION\
==================================================\
\
Create an About section on the homepage.\
\
Explain:\
- What the marketplace is\
- What problem it solves\
- The type of digital products available\
- The platform's philosophy\
- Security/reliability principles\
\
Keep the writing sophisticated and concise.\
\
Use terminal-inspired headings such as:\
\
$ cat about.txt\
\
ABOUT\
\
Do not make the content sound like fake cybersecurity marketing.\
\
==================================================\
11. SECURITY / TRUST SECTION\
==================================================\
\
Create a section explaining the platform's approach to secure transactions.\
\
It should communicate concepts such as:\
\
- Secure authentication\
- Protected payment processing\
- Server-side payment verification\
- Account activation after payment verification\
- Secure handling of payment information\
\
Do NOT claim certifications or security guarantees that have not actually been implemented.\
\
The UI should communicate trust without making unsupported claims.\
\
==================================================\
12. FAQ SECTION\
==================================================\
\
Create a terminal-style FAQ.\
\
Example:\
\
$ help\
\
[+] How does purchasing work?\
[+] How are payments processed?\
[+] When does my account become active?\
[+] What happens if my payment is still processing?\
[+] What happens if I lose internet during payment?\
[+] What happens if my payment fails?\
[+] How do I contact support?\
\
Use expandable accordion interactions.\
\
==================================================\
13. CONTACT SECTION\
==================================================\
\
Create a Contact section on the homepage.\
\
Example:\
\
$ contact support\
\
Need assistance?\
\
[ Email Support ]\
\
[ Contact Support ]\
\
The exact contact mechanism should remain configurable.\
\
Do not invent email addresses.\
\
