==================================================\
18. REGISTER\
==================================================\
\
Route:\
\
/register\
\
Terminal-inspired Firebase Authentication registration screen.\
\
Fields:\
- Username\
- Email\
- Password\
- Confirm password\
- Terms agreement\
\
After registration:\
\
Firebase Authentication creates the account.\
\
Firestore user record should use the existing architecture.\
\
Initial account status:\
\
pending_payment\
\
The frontend must not manually mark the account active.\
\
==================================================\
19. LOGIN\
==================================================\
\
Route:\
\
/login\
\
Fields:\
\
Email\
Password\
\
Actions:\
\
[ LOGIN ]\
[ FORGOT PASSWORD ]\
[ BACK ]\
\
Use Firebase Authentication.\
\
==================================================\
20. CHECKOUT / PAYMENT\
==================================================\
\
Route:\
\
/checkout/:orderId\
\
Display:\
\
Product\
Price\
Currency\
Payment method\
Payment status\
\
Example:\
\
root@marketplace:~/checkout#\
\
PAYMENT SESSION\
----------------------------\
\
PRODUCT     : Product Name\
PRICE       : $49.00\
PAYMENT     : Cryptocurrency\
PROCESSOR   : NOWPayments\
\
STATUS      : READY\
\
[ PROCEED TO PAYMENT ]\
\
The frontend calls the existing Firebase Cloud Function.\
\
The Cloud Function creates the NOWPayments hosted invoice.\
\
The function returns the invoice URL.\
\
React redirects the user to NOWPayments.\
\
IMPORTANT:\
\
React must NEVER determine payment success.\
\
Do not activate accounts based on:\
- Redirect URL\
- success_url\
- Client-side state\
- Browser state\
- User clicking a button\
\
Payment status comes from the backend/Firestore architecture already defined.\
\
==================================================\
21. PAYMENT STATUS UI\
==================================================\
\
The UI must support the backend payment states.\
\
Examples:\
\
WAITING\
PROCESSING\
COMPLETED\
UNDERPAID\
FAILED\
EXPIRED\
REFUNDED\
\
Display these states clearly.\
\
Example:\
\
PAYMENT STATUS\
----------------------------\
\
Provider Status : confirming\
System Status   : processing\
\
[ WAITING FOR CONFIRMATION ]\
\
When completed:\
\
PAYMENT STATUS\
----------------------------\
\
Provider Status : finished\
System Status   : completed\
\

\f3 \uc0\u10003 
\f0  PAYMENT VERIFIED\
\
ACCOUNT STATUS : ACTIVE\
\
The frontend simply reflects backend state.\
\
