\
==================================================\
28. INTERACTION PRINCIPLES\
==================================================\
\
The website should LOOK like a terminal.\
\
It should NOT force users to USE a terminal.\
\
Normal actions should be clickable.\
\
For example:\
\
[ VIEW PRODUCT ]\
\
[ PURCHASE ]\
\
[ LOGIN ]\
\
[ REGISTER ]\
\
[ PROCEED TO PAYMENT ]\
\
The command-line language is visual branding.\
\
Optionally, command-style interactions can be added as progressive enhancement later.\
\
==================================================\
29. ANIMATION PRINCIPLES\
==================================================\
\
Use subtle animations:\
\
- Blinking cursor\
- Small hover transitions\
- Status transitions\
- Page transitions\
- Loading indicators\
- Expand/collapse FAQ\
\
Avoid excessive animation.\
\
Performance is more important than visual effects.\
\
==================================================\
30. ACCESSIBILITY\
==================================================\
\
Despite the terminal aesthetic:\
\
- Maintain readable contrast\
- Use semantic HTML\
- Keyboard navigation must work\
- Buttons must be actual buttons\
- Links must be actual links\
- Inputs must have labels\
- Focus states must be visible\
- Do not rely solely on color to communicate status\
- Mobile touch targets must be comfortable\
\
